#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:76
msgid "OpenFermion"
msgstr "OpenFermion"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:78
msgid ""
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.openfermion` converts between an OpenFermion "
"``QubitOperator`` and a QiliSDK "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.Hamiltonian`, which lets you build a "
"problem with OpenFermion's chemistry tooling and then evolve or optimize it "
"with QiliSDK."
msgstr ""
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.openfermion` convierte entre un ``QubitOperator`` de "
"OpenFermion y un :class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.Hamiltonian` de "
"QiliSDK, lo que te permite construir un problema con las herramientas de "
"química de OpenFermion y después evolucionarlo u optimizarlo con QiliSDK."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:82
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.openfermion_to_qilisdk` — "
"build a Hamiltonian from a ``QubitOperator``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.openfermion_to_qilisdk` — "
"construir un hamiltoniano a partir de un ``QubitOperator``."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:83
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.qilisdk_to_openfermion` — "
"build a ``QubitOperator`` from a Hamiltonian."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.qilisdk_to_openfermion` — "
"construir un ``QubitOperator`` a partir de un hamiltoniano."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:85
msgid ""
"Each term of the ``QubitOperator`` becomes a product of "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliX`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliY` and "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliZ` operators on the corresponding "
"qubits. OpenFermion's empty term, which stands for the identity, becomes "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliI` on qubit 0."
msgstr ""
"Cada término del ``QubitOperator`` se convierte en un producto de operadores"
" :class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliX`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliY` y "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliZ` sobre los cúbits "
"correspondientes. El término vacío de OpenFermion, que representa la "
"identidad, se convierte en :class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.PauliI` sobre"
" el cúbit 0."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:100
#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:115
msgid "**Output**::"
msgstr "**Salida**::"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:104
msgid ""
"The reverse direction drops identity factors, since OpenFermion writes the "
"identity as the empty term, and stores every coefficient as a complex "
"number."
msgstr ""
"La dirección inversa descarta los factores identidad, ya que OpenFermion "
"escribe la identidad como el término vacío, y guarda todos los coeficientes "
"como números complejos."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_interoperability.rst:122
msgid ""
"Only the qubit-operator representation is converted. An OpenFermion "
"``FermionOperator`` has to be mapped to qubits first (with "
"``jordan_wigner``, ``bravyi_kitaev`` or any other OpenFermion transform) "
"before it can be handed to "
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.openfermion_to_qilisdk`."
msgstr ""
"Solo se convierte la representación como operador de cúbits. Un "
"``FermionOperator`` de OpenFermion debe mapearse primero a cúbits (con "
"``jordan_wigner``, ``bravyi_kitaev`` o cualquier otra transformación de "
"OpenFermion) antes de poder pasarlo a "
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.openfermion.openfermion.openfermion_to_qilisdk`."
